# Naming conventions

## Files & directories

| Item | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Directories | `kebab-case` | `apps/web/`, `packages/data/` |
| TypeScript source files | `kebab-case.ts` (NestJS suffixes allowed) | `incidents.service.ts`, `jwt.guard.ts`, `dispatch.gateway.ts` |
| React component files | `PascalCase.tsx` | `IncidentPanel.tsx`, `StatusPill.tsx` |
| Test files (unit) | colocated `*.spec.ts` | `incidents.service.spec.ts` |
| Test files (integration) | `apps/<app>/test/*.e2e-spec.ts` | `auth.e2e-spec.ts` |
| Static JSON content | `kebab-case.json` | `fire-service.json`, `cross-branch.json` |
| Prisma migrations | timestamp + `snake_case` description | `20260520143012_add_alliance_treasury/` |
| Env variable names | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET` |
| Public Next.js env | prefix `NEXT_PUBLIC_` | `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` |
| Markdown docs | `kebab-case.md` | `dispatch-one-mvp-implementation-spec.md` |

## Code identifiers

| Item | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| TypeScript types & interfaces | `PascalCase` | `IncidentTemplate`, `VehicleDef` |
| TypeScript variables & functions | `camelCase` | `computeWorkDuration`, `tryClaimVehicle` |
| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `ONE_GAME_MONTH_MS` |
| React components | `PascalCase` | `<RequirementsTable />` |
| Hooks | `useCamelCase` | `useGameClock`, `useT` |
| Vehicle / skill / incident / course IDs | ASCII `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `HLF_20`, `OPS_INCIDENT_CAP`, `FIRE_05`, `BREATHING_APPARATUS` |
| WebSocket event names | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `CONFIRM_DISPATCH`, `INCIDENT_SPAWNED` |
| Redis key namespaces | `kebab-case` with `:` segments | `lock:vehicle:{id}`, `player:{id}:inventory` |

## Database (Prisma)

- Model names: `PascalCase` (`Player`, `AllianceMessage`)
- Table names: `snake_case` via `@@map` (`players`, `alliance_messages`)
- Column names: `snake_case` via `@map` (`assigned_vehicle_id`, `created_at`)
- Enum values: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` (`EN_ROUTE`, `INCIDENT_COMPLETED`)

## ID normalisation

The user-facing display "HLF 20" maps to the canonical ID `HLF_20`. Never use the display form anywhere in code, JSON, types, or DB. `packages/utils/normalizeVehicleTypeId(display)` is the single converter.

## Anti-patterns

```typescript
// ❌ file naming
IncidentsService.ts     → ✅ incidents.service.ts
incident_panel.tsx      → ✅ IncidentPanel.tsx

// ❌ ID format
const id = 'hlf-20';    → ✅ const id = 'HLF_20';
const id = 'HLF 20';    → ✅ const id = 'HLF_20';
```
